# R5C-METAL-PREFILL-ARM — the `--model-forward-gpu` arm over the same synthetic two-layer model
#
# `docs/specs/r5c-metal-prefill.md` section 5.1. This block extends the existing runner rather than
# adding a target: `layer-forward-smoke` is already a member of HOSTED_CHECK_TARGETS, so R5C adds
# rows to it and changes no aggregate membership and no check topology.
#
# Hosted, ggml-free, **GPU-free**, model-free, llama.cpp-free. The default stub is unavailable and
# stops the arm at step 20 exactly as it stops `--model-forward`; the `engine` build is available
# and has no GPU device, which is `R5C_GPU_UNAVAILABLE` at step 20a; and three `engine+gpu*` builds
# give it one, take its host-pointer capability away, and shrink its maximum buffer length, so all
# three of the arm's new codes and its whole successful path are reached on a host with no GPU.
