    # only because a one-token prefill computed the embedding of token 0 whatever the operand said;
    # MF-SINGLE-TOKEN-LOGITS (roadmap item 36) fixed that, so `ds-suffix-prefix-one` moved to
    # `BOUNDARY_CASES` below as a passing oracle-S run at `T_prefix = 1`. Nothing replaced the check:
    # the sequence cap below is the only bound on `T_prefix`, which is why it is now the first
    # `R6_SUFFIX` a too-short-prefix caller can reach.
    # The **sequence** cap, `T_prefix + S <= MAX_PREFILL_TOKENS`. It is on the sequence and not on
    # `S` because the cap is the oracle's: oracle C'' runs `--model-forward` at `TOKENS,SUFFIX`, so a
    # cap on `S` alone would let the arm accept a run whose own acceptance oracle it refuses.
    ("ds-suffix-over-cap",
     ds(load=KV_GOOD, tokens=SUFFIX_PREFIX_TOKENS, suffix=",".join(["5"] * 2047)), "R6_SUFFIX"),
    # Precedence: step 3 precedes 3c, because `T_prefix` must be a number before `T_prefix + S` is
    # one, so both operands invalid names `R6_TOKENS`.
    ("ds-suffix-and-bad-tokens",
     ds(load=KV_GOOD, tokens=",".join(["1"] * 2049), suffix=SUFFIX_ONE), "R6_TOKENS"),
    # Precedence: 3c precedes 6, for the same sentence one term later.
    ("ds-suffix-over-cap-and-narrow",
     ds(load=KV_GOOD, tokens=SUFFIX_PREFIX_TOKENS, suffix=",".join(["5"] * 2047), width="4"),
     "R6_SUFFIX"),
    # The plane bound, **widened rather than duplicated**: step 6 reads
    # `T_prefix + S + N <= KV_WIDTH` and raises the code R6 already owns for "the plane is too
    # narrow for this run". Two codes for one condition is how two documents come to disagree.
    ("ds-suffix-narrow-width",
     ds(load=KV_GOOD, tokens=SUFFIX_PREFIX_TOKENS, suffix=SUFFIX_THREE, steps="2", width="6"),
     "R6_KV_WIDTH"),
]

